value.claim:
Relations: a schema may declare rel on any link field (single or array items);
the five built-in rels parse, resolve, and are exposed on the resolved schema;
an unknown rel string is accepted and behaves as ref;
dd graph map labels edges with their rel and can filter by it;
the built-in set is frozen in the surface manifest (docs/plans/065-deterministic-documents/tasks/phase-1-dd-core-foundations/dd-surface.md, one-line renegotiation to extend);
AND every existing builder/* link field declares its rel (pressure→pressure, proven_by→proven_by, done→derives, satisfies→satisfies), pinned by a schema test, so the engine is live on real plans from day one.

Links bucket: any list-item shape may carry a links bucket (array of rel-ref links) without per-schema bespoke fields;
rendered as a final Links column only when at least one item in that list has entries;
edges appear in dd links / dd graph map;
absent bucket renders byte-identical to today.

Contradiction engine: harness plan validate warns whenever a gate-terminal item links (via proven_by, satisfies, or derives) to a checkable target that is not gate-terminal — written once against rels, never field names;
planted-bad fixtures prove each rel path fires;
consistent-open and evidence-ready-unclaimed stay silent.

Scoped validate: --address <address> scopes the semantic checks to the address's reachable closure (outbound + incoming satisfies for AC rows), reusing the P7 graph-map traversal;
scoped runs are always per-row (strict implied);
green = in-scope terminal + no contradictions + no stale bases in scope;
the phase gate itself stays on the cheap completion read.

Check-kind gate: a flow node may carry dd_link {check: plan-validate, address};
departure evaluates the semantic validator live, refuses on non-green quoting the findings verbatim, records --force as a defended override exactly as the completion gate does;
the completion-kind gate is unchanged;
both kinds share the untrusted-reading discipline.

dd-native authoring: 1b plan emits plan.dd.json (+ built sibling plan.dd.md) as THE plan document — no -plan.md exists in a dd-native plan folder — and 5 tasks emits assets/tasks/phase-N/tasks.dd.json with done_when lists and satisfies edges, adding the phase row's tasks link in the same stroke;
the flow discovers both;
the scripted end-to-end dry-run (create → JIT → refuse → green → depart) runs as the wiring phase’s exit (ph-7102).

PR surface: ship renders the dd-derived AC table into the PR body — state marks + resolved proven_by / pressure / incoming-satisfies as clickable references — generated from the corpus under docs/plans/archive/<ord>-<slug>/ (7b has already archived;
the #90 read-from-archive rule);
refuses to fabricate on an unclosed corpus.

Layout & archive: the dd-native plan root holds plan.dd.json, plan.dd.md, the-flow.json, the-flow.md, plus original-ask.md where one exists (the stated amendment to #90's allow-list: the dd pair REPLACES <slug>-plan.md);
task files under assets/tasks/phase-N/;
after the post-flight git mv the corpus is doctor-clean AND the archive step rewrites the flow's repo-root-anchored dd_link addresses (fromPath null — they would otherwise silently go stale).

Exemplar & docs: the exemplar upgrades to the new schemas — 18 of 26 dw- rows currently lack pressure and each gets a real link or not-applicable;
the exemplar keeps its teaching layout at docs/how/dd/exemplar/ (a corpus, not a plan folder — NOT re-homed);
docs/how/dd/ + baked docs cover the new surface;
just checks green;
warn trio at baseline.

Tooling taught where it's needed: the dd/plan command surface is documented at BOTH builder layers — (a) node instructions[] baked by template/expander so harness flow orient (re-read every turn) surfaces the right command positionally (phase nodes: scoped rehearsal + state updates;
last review: --complete, closure, verify-basis;
gates print their own --force etiquette on refusal);
(b) stage modules teach their seam's commands (5 tasks: authoring;
6/6a: state flips + rehearsal;
7: closure + --complete;
8: PR render).

A dry-run reader following only orient output + the current stage module never lacks a command this plan introduced.

Self-hosting: by the final review, plan 071's own corpus is fully dogfooded — backpressure.dd.json and execution-log.dd.json exist with AC rows carrying pressure/proven_by links;
per-phase task files exist with done_when lists (mandatory pressure honoured);
tasks carry rel-typed satisfies;
the flight plan carries real dd_link gates exercised by the actual journey with the evidence RECORDED where each side lives: at least one genuine refusal captured in telemetry (command_exit carrying the gate E-code — refusals write nothing to the flow by pinned invariant) and any force as the existing dd-gate-override flow event;
plan validate --complete runs green at the last review node's gate;
ship's PR renders this plan's own AC table.

The corpus is indistinguishable from one authored entirely by the finished feature — the plan is its own acceptance fixture.

dd read/write verb family: harness dd get returns the value at any address;
dd set / dd add / dd rm mutate documents with schema validation BEFORE write, automatic sibling rebuild, and CLI-minted collision-free ids (add --mint <prefix>);
the frozen dd surface manifest gains the four rows via the one-line renegotiation;
agents never hand-edit .dd.json again — the CLI is the writer, matching the flow doctrine.

